  "generated_text": "To find the circumradius \\( R \\) of a triangle with sides \\( a = 6 \\), \\( b = 8 \\), and \\( c = 10 \\), we can use the formula for the circumradius of a triangle:\n\n\\[\nR = \\frac{abc}{4K}\n\\]\n\nwhere \\( K \\) is the area of the triangle. First, we need to determine the area \\( K \\) of the triangle. Since the sides \\( 6 \\), \\( 8 \\), and \\( 10 \\) form a right triangle (as \\( 6^2 + 8^2 = 10^2 \\)), we can use the formula for the area of a right triangle:\n\n\\[\nK = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{height} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 6 \\times 8 = 24\n\\]\n\nNow, we substitute \\( a = 6 \\), \\( b = 8 \\), \\( c = 10 \\), and \\( K = 24 \\) into the circumradius formula:\n\n\\[\nR = \\frac{6 \\times 8 \\times 10}{4 \\times 24} = \\frac{480}{96} = 5\n\\]\n\nThus, the circumradius of the triangle is \\(\\boxed{5}\\).",
